Package: assignmentB2AprilRadford
Title: Count Missing Values for All Columns by Group
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: 
    person("April", "Radford", , "april.c.radford@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Counts the missing values in every column of a data frame,
    separately for each level of a grouping column. The function
    count_all_missing_by_group() is a lightweight wrapper around the
    group_by() and summarize() functions in 'dplyr', and returns one row
    per group so that it is easy to see where missing data is
    concentrated.
